    "turn_text": "on you. We're going to focus on the things that you're working on. And those of you listening, you're invited to be a part of it. If you have a question for Congressman Mike Simpson, he's joining us here in studio, 208, 336, 3700, pound, 670, and your Verizon Wireless phone, because the business of Congress hasn't stopped just because the DA and Trump has been charged with falsifying business records in the first degree. We'll hear about that later on next hour, but for right now, it's me, Congressman Simpson, you're invited to be a part of it next. You can be a part of the conversation, 208, 336, 3700, pound, 670 under Verizon Wireless Phone. We can go right back to Washington DC and talk about everything that you're trying to work on or everything that is going on right now. I have a local issue because, well, right down the road from us in your district, right up the road from me, by the way, I'm a constituent, so technically you're boss. I've always had a question about the chips act and the mass amount of money that was spent, you know, trying to re-institute and get the chips to be manufactured back here. And since the act, since the money, Micron's been laying people off. Micron's gone through periods where they've been downsizing on that. How much of that reaches back to you and your office ago? Did you know, was it misrepresented? Do you have questions as a follow-up?",
