    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "we have a real supply chain problem in this country, not just with chips, but with critical minerals, et cetera, et cetera. And we need to reverse that. And that was the intent of that. It was $50 billion. By the time they added everything onto it, it was a $250 billion bill. And I was, why am I going to vote for a bill that is $50 billion that I support, but have to vote for a bill that's $250 billion. That doesn't make sense because I didn't agree with the other $200 billion in this bill. So I voted against it. But what they were trying to do in this bill is the right thing. And Micron is investing, I can't remember how many billion, it's like $1.7 billion in this facility out here. And they're also investing in some other places and stuff. But that's what they do. I'd just like to get the chips manufacturing back into this country. I don't like having to go and order a car or trying to buy a car, but you can't buy one because they don't have the chips for it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_06",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
