    "turn_idx": 112,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, we spend a ton of money at predator control. The problem with the dams is it's not seals and stuff. It is predators that are harder to contain, but behind the dams you have, you don't have a river, you have four pools. And it takes salmon about three times as long to get up and down as it used to. And that means they're more susceptible to the predators in these pools and the warm water and stuff. But yes, we do a lot in predator control. I mean, spend millions of dollars in predator control at the mouth of the Columbia River and all the way up and down the river, as a matter of fact.",
